Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: do not promise a USB RX key-generation fence

CAN_REPLACE_PTK0 requires that no frame decrypted with the old key reach
mac80211 after DISABLE_KEY returns. The USB TX drain does not fence the
device RX FIFO, pending transfers and queued hardware-decrypted frames.
Their descriptors do not identify the temporal key incarnation.

Leave the capability unchanged for other transports. USB keeps its existing
TX drain and crypto processing; normal mac80211 rekey warning/queue flushing
and the userspace policy selected by the operator remain authoritative.
This is a capability correction, not a fix for an attributed rekey stall.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
@@ -2310,7 +2310,9 @@
 		hw->wiphy->n_iface_combinations = ARRAY_SIZE(rtw_iface_combs);
 	}
 
-	wiphy_ext_feature_set(hw->wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_CAN_REPLACE_PTK0);
+	/* USB RX completion does not fence plaintext from the preceding key. */
+	if (rtw_hci_type(rtwdev) != RTW_HCI_TYPE_USB)
+		wiphy_ext_feature_set(hw->wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_CAN_REPLACE_PTK0);
 	wiphy_ext_feature_set(hw->wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_SCAN_RANDOM_SN);
 	wiphy_ext_feature_set(hw->wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_SET_SCAN_DWELL);
 
